# Local development secrets for `wrangler dev`.
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (which is gitignored) and fill in real values:
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# For deployed environments use `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>` instead —
# never commit real values, and never put secrets in wrangler.jsonc "vars".

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: AI Gateway routing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When BOTH of these are set, requests are proxied to your AI Gateway's
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint, which enables multi-provider routing
# ({provider}/{model}, including openrouter/... and dynamic/{route}), caching,
# rate limiting, spend limits, guardrails and unified billing.
#
# When either is missing, the Worker falls back to the Workers AI binding, so
# the app still works with no gateway configured.
#
# These two are not secret and may instead live in wrangler.jsonc "vars".
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your-account-id
# AI_GATEWAY_ID=your-gateway-id

# Token for an authenticated AI Gateway. Sent as `cf-aig-authorization`.
# Required if your gateway has authentication enabled.
# CF_AIG_TOKEN=your-gateway-token

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: router access control
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The API key clients must present as `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.
# This is the value you paste into Cline / Cursor / Claude Code as their
# "API Key" when pointing them at this router.
#
# If unset, the router is OPEN — acceptable only behind Cloudflare Access or
# during local development. Set it before exposing the Worker publicly.
# ROUTER_API_KEY=generate-something-long-and-random
